-- title:
--   Base-point freeness of M^{⊗ 2} on an abelian variety
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $A$ be a scheme and $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ a morphism, and let $L$ be a relative group law on $f$, that is, a group structure on the sets $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of $T$-points over each $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, natural in $T$; assume $L$ is commutative, i.e. its multiplication on $T$-points is commutative for every $t$. Assume furthermore that $f$ satisfies the bundle of properties `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle`: $f$ is smooth, proper, each fibre $f^{-1}(s)$ is connected, and $f$ admits a relative group law. Let $\mathcal{M}$ be a module on $A$ which is invertible, meaning that every point of $A$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ on which the pullback of $\mathcal{M}$ along $U \hookrightarrow A$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of rings of $U$. Endow $\Gamma(A,\top)$ with the $k$-algebra structure coming from $f$ and $\Gamma(\mathcal{M},\top)$ with the resulting $k$-module structure, and assume $\dim_k \Gamma(\mathcal{M},\top) > 0$. Finally let $\mathcal{N}$ be a module on $A$ together with an isomorphism $\mathcal{N} \cong \mathcal{M} \otimes \mathcal{M}$. Then there exist $N \in \mathbb{N}$, global sections $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_N \in \Gamma(\mathcal{N},\top)$ and opens $U_0,\dots,U_N$ of $A$ whose supremum is $\top$, such that each $\sigma_i$ is a frame on $U_i$: for every open $W \le U_i$ the map $\Gamma(A,W) \to \Gamma(\mathcal{N},W)$, $g \mapsto g \cdot \sigma_i|_W$, is bijective.
--
--   This is the base-point freeness of $|2D|$ on an abelian variety: if an invertible sheaf $\mathcal{M}$ has a nonzero global section, then $\mathcal{M}^{\otimes 2}$ is generated by global sections, here expressed as a finite family of global sections of $\mathcal{N} \cong \mathcal{M}^{\otimes 2}$ each trivialising $\mathcal{N}$ on a member of an open cover of $A$. It is the base case for the corresponding statement about higher tensor powers, [`AlgebraicGeometry.Polarisation.exists_isFrameOn_iSup_eq_top_of_iso_tensorPow_of_finrank_pos`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Polarisation.exists_isFrameOn_iSup_eq_top_of_iso_tensorPow_of_finrank_pos), and feeds into the construction of polarisations on Jacobians.
